Actually, I recall the specific one now. The Sanitizer API allows `<style>` elements. The content of `<style>` is treated as text. But there's a bug: when the sanitizer serializes, it doesn't escape the content of `<style>`. So if you have:

```html
<style><img src=x onerror=alert(1)></style>
